      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-5263",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+(0)^{2}+\\frac{(0+1)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =1 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 1 \\\\ x & =2\\pm 1 \\\\ x & =1,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $\\left(1, 0, 0\\right)$ and $\\left(3, 0, 0\\right).$",
